why Every Horde quest of the Sunken Temple in one run, class quests and lead-ins included.

# The Sunken Temple's Horde quests in one guide: the pick-ups in Orgrimmar
# (each class's trainer too), Stonard, the Hinterlands, a round of Kalimdor
# (Feralas, Un'Goro Crater, Tanaris, Ratchet, and for some classes Azshara and
# Felwood), back to Stonard, one run, then the hand-ins. Steps already done
# are passed over, so the guide picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chains:
# - Fel'zerul's 1424 Pool of Tears -> 1429 The Atal'ai Exile -> 1444 Return to
#   Fel'Zerul -> 1445 The Temple of Atal'Hakkar (twenty Fetishes of Hakkar).
# - Witch Doctor Uzer'i's 3380 The Sunken Temple -> Marvon Rivetseeker's 3444
#   The Stone Circle -> 3446 Into the Depths and 3447 Secret of the Circle.
# - Larion's 4145 Larion and Muigin -> 4147 Marvon's Workshop -> Liv
#   Rizzlefix's 4146 Zapper Fuel -> 4148 Bloodpetal Zapper.
# - The Atal'ai Exile's 1446 Jammal'an the Prophet.
# - Yeh'kinya's 3528 The God Hakkar, for characters who handed in The Ancient
#   Egg (4787, in the Zul'Farrak guide).
# - The Essence of Eranikus (from the Shade of Eranikus) starts 3373.
# - Classes, each from its trainer in Orgrimmar (Druids in Thunder Bluff):
#   Hunters 8151 -> Ogtinc's 8153 -> 8231 -> 8232 The Green Drake; Rogues 8233
#   -> Lord Jorach Ravenholdt's 8234 -> Archmage Xylem's 8235 -> 8236 The
#   Azure Key; Mages 8250 -> Xylem's 8251 -> 8252 -> 8253 Destroy Morphaz;
#   Priests 8254 -> Ogtinc's 8255 -> 8256 -> 8257 Blood of Morphaz (to Greta
#   Mosshoof); Shamans 8410 -> Bath'rah the Windwatcher's 8412 -> 8413 Da
#   Voodoo; Warlocks 8419 -> Impsy's 8421 -> 8422 Trolls of a Feather;
#   Warriors 8417 -> the Fallen Hero of the Horde's 8423 -> 8424 -> 8425
#   Voodoo Feathers; Druids 9063 -> Torwa Pathfinder's 9052 -> 9051 -> 9053 A
#   Better Ingredient.
#
# Left out: 8733 Eranikus, Tyrant of the Dream (its chain needs Blackwing
# Lair); 3374, the Essence of Eranikus' second part (it starts from the
# Oathstone of Ysera's Dragonflight, not at the Essence Font); 5065 The Lost
# Tablets of Mosh'aru after The God Hakkar (another NPC gives it).
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, the troll mini-bosses, the
# haze mobs, the Altar or Idol of Hakkar or the Essence Font inside, so their
# goals stand at the door (@69.9,53.5, Swamp of Sorrows) with `group 5`. The
# bosses come in the order of the client's dungeon journal (Atal'alarion,
# Avatar of Hakkar, Shade of Eranikus, Hazzas, Morphaz, Weaver, Dreamscythe,
# Jammal'an the Prophet; Spawn of Hakkar and Ogom the Wretched optional), not
# of a recorded run. Every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a group
# that takes them in another order still gets each step ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The God Hakkar also needs the Essence of
#   Hakkar, which the Shade of Hakkar or the Avatar of Hakkar drops; the data
#   has no source for the Filled Egg itself. The voodoo feathers come from six
#   named trolls inside; the Fetishes of Hakkar from the temple's trolls,
#   inside and around it. Lint warns that the door is more than 50 yards
#   from the trolls outside; the goal stays at the door for the ones inside.
# - The door: QuestieDB's list of Forever's dungeons, as Polestar's Codex holds it
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   50 to 60). The client also lists a 20-player Sunken Temple; this guide is
#   the five-player dungeon's.
# INGAME: where inside do the Altar of Hakkar, the circle of statues, the
#   Essence Font, the six feather trolls and the haze mobs stand?

